Please move the debug log in `if (hostname)` block. Also, as already commented in the above, `USE_HOSTNAME_BOTH` is meaningless, so how about something like the following:
```
if (hostname) {
    log_link_debug(link, "Setting...");
    r = manager_set_hostname(link->manager, hostname, link->network->dhcp_use_hostname == USE_HOSTNAME_STATIC);
    if (r < 0)
         log_link_error_errno(...);
}
```

Then, 
```
if (static_hostname)
    r = free_and_strdup(&m->static_hostname, hostname);
else
    r = free_and_strdup(&m->transient_hostname, hostname);
if (r < 0)
    return log_oom();
```

If `bus` is not ready when setting hostname at first, then, this always try to set transient hostname...

How about the following?
```
# networkd-manager.h
Manager {
    (...);
    char *transient_hostname;
    char *static_hostname;
    (...);
}

# networkd-manager.c
if (m->static_hostname)
    (void) manager_set_hostname(m, m->static_hostname, true);
else if (m->transient_hostname)
    (void) manager_set_hostname(m, m->transient_hostname, false);
```
